# Same domain as production: not a secret, and there is only one pool.
#
# `npm run dev` cannot sign in, and filling `VITE_CLIENT_ID` in here does not
# change that — it makes it worse. The client registers one callback URL,
# `https://vanessa.matteo.cool/`, and the browser always asks to come back to
# `location.origin`, so from the dev server managed login answers
# `redirect_mismatch` on its own page and never returns. Left empty, the app
# stops earlier and more clearly, on the "configurazione mancante" guard in
# auth.ts.
#
# Registering `http://localhost:5173/` on the pool would not fix it either:
# the dev proxy in vite.config.ts points `/api` at the API Gateway hostname,
# which refuses anything without the origin secret CloudFront injects, so a
# working sign-in would land in an app that 401s on every call. See "«npm run
# dev» non fa accedere" in app/README.md.
VITE_LOGIN_DOMAIN=https://auth.vanessa.matteo.cool
VITE_CLIENT_ID=
